WEBVTT

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:06.200
Using traveling stitches to frame eyelets
can create a beautiful, decorative

00:00:06.233 --> 00:00:08.570
stitch pattern for your knitting.

00:00:08.603 --> 00:00:13.960
As machine knitters, because the purl side
faces us as we knit, this can

00:00:13.993 --> 00:00:16.600
be a bit confusing at first.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:21.950
This is one of those techniques
that you have to try it to get it.

00:00:21.983 --> 00:00:26.370
The secret is to get a mental picture
of the effect from the knit side

00:00:26.403 --> 00:00:29.720
or the finished side of the work.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.690
To make the stitches travel,
we'll work a two-step transfer.

00:00:34.723 --> 00:00:38.160
First, we'll identify
the traveling stitch.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:43.240
Then transfer the stitch next to it,
doubling up the stitches.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:48.600
Then move both stitches
to fill that emptied needle.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.930
This transfer empties the eyelet needle.

00:00:52.963 --> 00:00:58.150
Make sure you keep that eyelet
needle in work and knit two rows.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:03.970
Next, identify  that traveling stitch
again by following your chart,

00:01:04.003 --> 00:01:09.410
and you can also reach underneath and feel
the bulk of that traveling stitch.

00:01:09.443 --> 00:01:16.520
Transfer the stitch next to it, doubling
up the stitches and emptying a needle.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:22.570
Take both of those stitches and transfer
them to fill the emptied needle.

00:01:22.603 --> 00:01:26.650
Moving these two stitches
empties the eyelet needle.

00:01:26.683 --> 00:01:32.170
Make sure that that eyelet needle
remains in work and knit two rows.

00:01:32.203 --> 00:01:35.250
You'll continue this
for the stitch pattern.

00:01:35.283 --> 00:01:39.250
Now, you can also keep track
of the traveling stitch by needle number

00:01:39.283 --> 00:01:41.570
by creating a chart.

00:01:41.603 --> 00:01:45.160
Use Knitter's Graph paper and draw out
what you want your traveling

00:01:45.193 --> 00:01:47.617
stitches to look like.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.770
Your best bet is to try this on a swatch.

00:01:50.803 --> 00:01:55.320
Once you take it off the machine,
the light bulb will come on and you can

00:01:55.353 --> 00:02:01.080
get creative with positioning
traveling eyelets across your knitting.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:07.010
Don't forget that these eyelets are going
to impact your stitch and row gauge,

00:02:07.043 --> 00:02:09.920
so be sure to swatch in pattern.

